From b4d9101b01e7a20773faf050479a45a3bfdf2d73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kim Eun Ju <kejgood77@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:28:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep one light look and a fixed text size

The 2026-09-30 decisions dropped dark mode and dynamic type for now, but
the app still followed the system for both.

- app.json userInterfaceStyle: automatic -> light. Android needs
  expo-system-ui for this to apply; it is not installed yet and is
  noted in HANDOFF for the development-build switch.
- PixelText, PixelInput and MemoEditor set allowFontScaling={false}.
  RN Web ignores the prop, so Storybook and vitest cannot show it;
  check on a device with the largest text size.

HANDOFF also records that the fixed-header scroll was confirmed on the
user's iPhone 15 Pro.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
